  "name": "coupled_wing_switch",
  "description": "One-input coupled wing. The upper arm is bolted to the body (it is the ground frame, 0.30 m from the shoulder at the origin to the elbow). Forearm of two bones, ulna 0.35 m / 0.12 kg and radius 0.35 m / 0.04 kg, pinned 2 cm apart to the upper arm and to the hand (0.25 m / 0.06 kg): a parallelogram, so the hand stays parallel to the upper arm while the elbow folds. Elbow stops (k 100 N m/rad, c 2.5 N m s/rad) at open (0 degrees) and folded (-150 degrees). An elastic ligament (EA 200 N, c 5 N s/m) crosses the elbow and passes over it at -75 degrees, so it presses the elbow into the nearer stop with at least 0.5 N m beyond the wing\u0027s weight: the wing rests open and rests folded with the elbow servo idle. Standard gravity. The servo pushes the elbow toward folding with 2 N m for 0.15 s from 0.05 s (10 ms ramps), then lets go: the elbow is past the over-center angle, and the ligament finishes the fold and holds it on the folded stop. From 0.5 s the same pulse the other way opens the wing again. Between and after the pulses the servo is idle and the wing is locked.",
